WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.860
<u></u>Planet Castrop

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:07.530
<i>Lord Eugen Castrop, the ruler of the 
Castrop Starzone in the Galactic Empire,</i>

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:11.390
<i>served as minister of finance 
under Kaiser Friedrich IV.</i>

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.820
<i>He served for fifteen years,</i>

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.320
<i>during which time he embezzled 
vast amounts of money.</i>

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.670
<i>But when Lord Castrop unexpectedly 
died in an accident,</i>

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.930
<i>the truth of his embezzlement 
came to light.</i>

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.330
<i>The Empire's Ministries 
of Finance and Justice</i>

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.060
<i>attempted to take away his 
unlawfully accumulated riches.</i>

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.330
<i>However...</i>

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.340
<u></u>Franz von Mariendorf

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.090
<i>Lord Castrop's son, 
Maximilian, pushed back.</i>

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.850
<i>And thus the Castrop Rebellion began.</i>

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:45.850
<u></u>Maximilian von Castrop

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.640
<i>Meanwhile, the Empire's new 
fleet admiral, Reinhard,</i>

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.370
<u></u>Fleet Admiral's Mansion

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.610
<i>established the Fleet Admiral's Mansion,</i>

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:04.690
<i>in which he assembled all of the Imperial 
Navy's top up-and-coming commanders.</i>

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:10.410
<i>This assembly received an imperial 
order from Kaiser Friedrich IV...</i>

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.110
Rear Admiral Siegfried Kircheis.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:13.980
Sir.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:21.710
You will depart for the Castrop Starzone 
to suppress a rebellion.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:22.500
Yes, sir.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.610
I humbly accept this assignment.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:58.030
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:05.030
There seems to be some bias in 
Count Lohengramm's appointments.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.750
Private Secretary Weitz

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.650
All of the officers he's assembled are 
commoners and low-ranking nobles.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:15.030
And can Rear Admiral Kircheis really 
handle the matter with Castrop?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.360
Would Count Lohengramm 
not be a better choice?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.510
<u>Minister of State and Acting Prime Minister of the Galactic Empire
</u>Klaus von Lichtenlade

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.550
It was Count Lohengramm who requested that 
the order be given to Rear Admiral Kircheis.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.220
Is it such a bad thing?

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.280
Rear Admiral Kircheis is the 
count's most trusted confidant.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:34.040
If we grant him a reward for success in 
this mission, he'll be indebted to us,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.140
which will be beneficial to us later.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.090
And if he fails,

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.110
the responsibility will fall on 
Count Lohengramm for recommending him.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:47.530
If his subordinate fails, the count will 
have one less thing to brag about.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.080
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.080
<b>The Castrop Rebellion</b>

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.000
Vice Admiral Fritz Joseph Bittenfeld

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.000
Why would that upstart 
receive an imperial order?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.030
The count must have pulled some strings.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:03.090
Vice Admiral Karl Gustav Kempff

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:04.460
Siegfried Kircheis... 
What sort of man will he prove to be?

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.000
Many of the soldiers seem 
to have their doubts

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.930
as to whether he's a man they 
can entrust their lives to.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:15.220
Why would Count Lohengramm be 
so close to someone like him?

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.770
Vice Admiral Cornelius Lutz

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.890
The two of them have been 
friends since childhood.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.960
If that's true, then I was wrong 
about the count all this time.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.860
I thought he had great potential.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.250
I wonder what those other 
two think of this.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:31.500
Vice Admiral August Samuel Wahlen

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.330
You mean Vice Admirals 
Reuenthal and Mittermeyer?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.880
They fought under the count in the past.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:38.630
<u></u>Vice Admiral Ernest Mecklinger

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.090
They probably know 
Rear Admiral Kircheis well, too.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.890
Vice Admiral Wolfgang Mittermeyer

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.210
How much have you heard about 
the Castrop Rebellion?

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.970
The rebellion is still ongoing.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.940
<u></u>Vice Admiral Oskar von Reuenthal

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:58.220
If he can stop it, Kircheis will 
be promoted to vice admiral.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:01.310
That would put him at the same rank as us,

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.930
and would no doubt put him 
well ahead of the pack.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.110
Perhaps the count wants to let everyone 
in his mansion and beyond know

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.020
that Kircheis is his number two.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.850
Think it'll work out?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.110
Who knows?

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:19.310
But if the count thinks he and Kircheis...

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:23.160
no, if he thinks we all need this to 
happen in order to meet our goal...

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.130
Then we have no choice 
but to trust and obey.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:31.510
The count kept his promise by inviting us to 
the Fleet Admiral's Mansion he established.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.600
We should keep our promise, too.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.880
Right. All we can do is remain loyal.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:43.940
<i>Kircheis...</i>

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.740
<u>Kircheis Fleet Flagship
</u>Barbarossa

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.290
Captain Volker Axel von Bülow

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.880
Captain Hans Eduard Bergengrün

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:06.200
The Imperial Navy is advancing 
in our direction.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.930
I can see that!

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.840
They only number 5,000. 
We'll tear them apart!

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.930
Castrop Fleet approaching.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.340
They number approximately 10,000.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.990
Commence the operation.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.140
The Imperial Navy is 
approaching at high speed!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.860
Commence attack!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.690
The enemy is attempting to surround 
us rather than counterattack.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:51.240
Using 5,000 ships to surround 
10,000? They really are fools.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.010
They don't know basic strategy!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.460
We should counterattack.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.180
Our shields can't take any more!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.120
There's a gap in the enemy's 
encirclement at eleven o'clock.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.960
Have all remaining ships charge into it.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.860
Wait, please. Basic strategy
is what the enemy is using.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:12.890
The enemy wants to lure us to that 
point and take all of us out at once.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.070
Some sacrifices are unavoidable.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:20.620
To give one's life for his 
master is a retainer's honor!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.160
Give the order to charge!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.030
Enemy fleet is relocating to five o'clock.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.980
Your Excellency, we need an all-out attack.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.120
Remain on the defensive.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:47.970
When they think we're faltering, 
we'll let them pass through.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.680
Close the gap!

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.220
Bring us in front of the enemy flagship!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.170
Message from the Imperial Navy.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:47.290
Open the line!

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.550
<i>Message to all Castrop Navy fleets.</i>

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:55.730
<i>I am Rear Admiral Siegfried Kircheis 
of the Galactic Imperial Navy.</i>

00:08:56.430 --> 00:09:00.290
<i>Our objective in this mission 
is to detain Maximilian Castrop,</i>

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:03.390
<i>the leader of the rebellion.</i>

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.840
<i>The officers and soldiers 
of the Castrop Navy</i>

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.400
<i>did no more than fight as their 
leader instructed them.</i>

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.000
If you resist no further,

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.940
you will be given fair treatment 
as prisoners of war,

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:18.690
and I will give you my word that we will 
not take your lives for pleasure.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:23.410
<i>The fact that I did not sink a single 
ship should prove my sincerity to you.</i>

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.120
The fool!

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:39.020
Order the ships at the front line 
to attack the enemy fleet!

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.710
We'll catch them in a pincer attack!

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:55.930
What are you doing?! Attack the enemy!

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:59.990
We aren't the ones in danger! They are!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.240
Do you not understand?! A pincer attack!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.130
Fire the main cannons! Fire! Fire!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.270
Why won't you fire?!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.010
Fire! Fire!

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:12.470
Our allies haven't returned.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.070
If we attack, we'll destroy our 
forces within their encirclement.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:18.100
How dare you talk back to me?!

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.570
You have some nerve for a former commoner!

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.440
Fire now! Fire, I say!

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.380
I am your master! 
I am Lord Maximilian Castrop!

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:41.380
You said it was a retainer's honor 
to give his life for his master,

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:46.540
but I believe it's a master's job to 
give of his own life for his people.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.480
Message from the Castrop Navy flagship.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.160
"Maximilian Castrop is dead.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:11.760
We accept your recommendation 
of surrender."

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:12.770
Dead?

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:13.680
It can't be...

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.680
We will proceed toward Planet Castrop.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.610
Caution the men to handle 
the prisoners with care,

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:26.310
and not to engage in looting or other 
activity that may harm civilians.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.110
Any violation of military regulations 
will be severely punished.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.220
Yes, sir!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.500
He put down the rebellion?!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.000
In just ten days?!

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.030
No, actual combat only lasted two days.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.850
Proceeding to
Castrop took six days,

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.460
and follow-up procedures took two days.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.460
I guess he does deserve to 
be at the count's side.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:02.060
Salute Rear Admiral Siegfried Kircheis!

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.960
Vice Admiral Kircheis.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.910
Strive for ever greater loyalty to His Imperial 
Majesty the Kaiser in gratitude for his favor.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:13.980
Yes, sir.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:18.850
<i>For ever greater loyalty, huh?</i>

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.580
<i>The one I swear my loyalty to is...</i>

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:38.910
Enter.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:45.290
We've received an urgent 
message from headquarters.

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:46.280
What is it?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.370
Sir, Iserlohn has...

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.260
Iserlohn Fortress has fallen.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.630
<u>Galactic Empire  Military Chief of Staff
</u>Fleet Admiral Ehrenberg

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:02.900
What?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:07.260
Wasn't Iserlohn supposed to be impregnable?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.260
I can't believe it!

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.560
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy  Chief of Headquarters
</u>Fleet Admiral Steinhof

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.600
Could the report have been mistaken?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:17.450
Seeckt is dead, 
and Stockhausen is in enemy hands.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:18.650
<u>Galactic Imperial Navy  Space Fleet Chief Commander
</u>Fleet Admiral Mückenberger

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:21.980
But someone has to take 
responsibility for this defeat.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.610
Which means...

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:32.090
Imperial territory must be kept 
inviolable to outside invasion,

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:34.280
and until now, it has always been so.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:38.920
The situation that troubles Your Majesty's mind

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:45.280
is entirely the result of my own failures,

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.730
and I am deeply ashamed.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.790
That's a funny argument, Kircheis.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:54.810
Yes, sir.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:14:00.980
We aren't supposed to give even an inch of 
Imperial territory to outside invaders.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:05.110
When did the rebels become an outside 
force of strength equal to ours?

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:09.070
Failing to see reality gives 
rise to contradictions.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:13.930
And what is the name of the Alliance 
commander who took down Iserlohn?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.480
The Free Planets Alliance 
13th Fleet commander,

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:21.110
Rear Admiral Yang Wen-li.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:25.120
It's the man from Astarte again.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.040
Yang Wen-li...

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:33.010
Enter.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.880
Someone requests an audience 
with Your Excellency.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.930
We will take him from here. Wait out front.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:59.700
I can't go anywhere without 
military police accompaniment.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.980
Captain Oberstein, correct?

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:05.920
What business do you have with me?

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.950
First, please clear the room.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:12.010
There are only three of us here.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.190
Yes, Vice Admiral Kircheis is here.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:18.470
This is why I asked you to clear the room.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.990
Vice Admiral Kircheis should 
be considered the same as me.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.880
You don't know that?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.360
I do.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.770
This is something you still 
don't want him to hear, then.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:33.060
But I'll just tell him later, 
and the result will be the same.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.040
Of course, Your Excellency 
is free to do so.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:42.280
However, achieving supremacy requires 
a variety of different people.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:44.980
You tell A things that A needs to know,

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:47.270
and you give B an assignment suited to B.

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:49.510
I believe this is how certain 
matters should be conducted.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:55.260
Your Excellency, perhaps I 
should wait in the next room.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.240
Very well.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:12.110
The truth, Your Excellency, is that I 
currently stand in a difficult position.

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:14.140
I believe you are aware of this.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:18.400
You're a deserter from Iserlohn. 
It's natural you would be condemned.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.560
Especially when Admiral Seeckt 
died such an honorable death.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:27.480
I'm sure the many commanders see me 
as no more than a cowardly deserter.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.230
But, Your Excellency, I do have 
my reasons for what I did.

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.630
I would like you to hear them.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.250
This is absurd.

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:38.620
If you insist on explaining, 
don't explain to me.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.610
Explain at tomorrow's court-martial.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:43.680
A court-martial is only for show.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:47.430
My punishment has been 
decided from the start.

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.120
Please look at this, Your Excellency.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.520
As I believe Vice Admiral 
Kircheis informed you,

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:01.050
both of my eyes are artificial.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.610
Under Emperor Rudolf's rule,

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:08.910
I would have been killed as an infant 
under the Inferior Genes Exclusion Act.

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:11.700
Do you understand?

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:14.200
I despise him.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:17.000
I despise Emperor Rudolf, his descendants,

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.510
and everything he created.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.640
I despise the Goldenbaum Dynasty itself.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.930
That's a very bold statement.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:33.390
The Galactic Empire... 
no, the Goldenbaum Dynasty should fall.

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:37.140
If possible, I would love to 
bring about its demise myself.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:41.150
However, I lack the capacity to do so.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:45.860
All I can do is collaborate in the 
establishment of a new supreme ruler,

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.330
and that is all.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:52.540
I'm talking about you, Your Excellency the 
Fleet Admiral, Count Reinhard Lohengramm.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:53.540
Kircheis.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:57.770
Hand Captain Oberstein over 
to the military police.

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.300
He has made rebellious statements 
toward the Empire.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:04.220
As an Imperial soldier, 
I can't overlook this.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.150
I guess that's all there is to you...

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:17.130
Fine. Depend on Vice Admiral Kircheis 
as your only trusted confidant,

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.570
and continue to walk down your narrow path.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:25.360
Vice Admiral Kircheis, can you shoot me?

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.140
As you can see, I'm completely unarmed.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.500
Can you still shoot me?

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.470
You can't, can you? 
That's the kind of man you are.

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:40.610
You're worthy of respect, but that 
isn't enough to achieve supremacy.

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.570
The shadow follows the light...

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:49.510
But perhaps the young Count Lohengramm 
doesn't yet understand this.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.000
You're a man who says 
what he pleases, I see.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:58.940
Forgive me.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:03.720
Seeckt must have hated you. Am I wrong?

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:08.950
Admiral Seeckt was not a man who 
inspired loyalty in his subordinates.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.390
Military Chief of Staff Ehrenberg,

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.720
Chief of Headquarters Steinhof,

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.690
and Space Fleet Chief 
Commander Mückenberger.

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:28.720
These three chiefs of staff have 
submitted their resignations

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.680
to assume responsibility 
for the loss of Iserlohn.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.970
Which position would you like?

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:38.650
Any commendations I've received
were not the result of my own efforts.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:42.620
I could not take another's position.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.260
The loss of Iserlohn was...

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:49.810
a result of mistakes made by 
Admirals Seeckt and Stockhausen.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:54.390
In addition, Admiral Seeckt atoned 
for his sin through death,

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:57.160
and the other has been 
imprisoned by the enemy.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:02.050
I do not feel that anyone 
else should accept blame.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:08.590
I humbly request that Your Majesty find 
no fault with the three chiefs of staff.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:13.960
I never thought I would owe a 
debt to the blond youngster.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.590
I understand he requested 
immunity for Oberstein

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:21.340
along with his transfer to the 
Fleet Admiral's Mansion.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:25.870
We can hardly accept His Imperial 
Majesty's generous favor

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.700
while allowing that man to 
be so harshly punished.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.490
Still, to voluntarily give up 
a chief of staff position

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.690
was a surprisingly selfless act.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:41.700
Forgive me, Your Imperial Majesty.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.620
What is it?

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:48.290
I realize this will displease you, but...

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.850
Is this about Lohengramm?

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:56.610
You want to tell me I've given too much 
prestige and power to Annerose's brother.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:21:00.250
Your Imperial Majesty is aware of this?

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.090
Since he is fearless,

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:06.400
he will not simply be satisfied with
the position of senior statesman,

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:11.520
but might get carried away and 
plot to usurp me. Am I right?

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:16.280
I hesitated to put such 
thoughts into words...

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.880
I see no problem with this.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:20.540
Pardon?

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:26.140
The Goldenbaum Dynasty has not existed 
since the creation of humanity.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:31.000
Just as no man is immortal, 
no country is infallible.

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:36.510
It would not be unreasonable for the 
Galactic Empire to end with my generation.

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.740
If it's going to fall anyway,

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:45.830
I would hope that it has a magnificent end.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:54.930
You look like you want to say something.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.130
You know what it is. You're being cruel.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:01.610
Don't get mad. It's about Oberstein, right?

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:05.380
You suspect he might be a 
pawn of some noble family.

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:07.520
I suspected the same, briefly.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:12.020
But he's not a man the nobles could handle.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:15.220
He's smart, but he's too peculiar.

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:19.360
And could you handle him, Reinhard?

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:23.320
A good question.

00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:28.500
I don't expect friendship 
or loyalty from him.

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:32.170
He's only trying to use me

00:22:32.170 --> 00:22:34.990
to achieve his own goals.

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:42.280
So I'm going to use his intellect in turn.

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:45.260
I don't care what his motives are.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.460
If I can't control one man,

00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:50.790
how could I ever expect to 
rule the whole universe?

00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:57.530
That's enough for today.

00:22:57.840 --> 00:22:59.020
You can go.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:22:59.810
Yes, sir.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.020
<i>Oberstein will be useful.</i>

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:12.120
<i>He won't hesitate to take 
any means necessary.</i>

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:15.470
<i>But still...</i>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>Each Person's Star</b>

00:24:50.530 --> 00:24:55.000
<i>Next time on </i>Legend of 
 the Galactic Heroes - Die Neue These<i>,</i>

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:58.730
<i>episode nine, "Each Person's Star."</i>
